Semiconductor packaging plays a critical role in protecting chips from moisture, mechanical stress and environmental exposure. Liquid molding compounds are used to encapsulate and protect semiconductor devices, with material properties influencing package reliability, manufacturing efficiency and long-term performance.

According to SemiconductorInsight, the global Liquid Molding Compounds (LMC) Market was valued at USD 585.1 million in 2025 and is projected to reach USD 1.06 billion by 2034, growing at a CAGR of 6.8% during 2026–2034. Asia Pacific leads the market, accounting for more than 60% of global consumption by volume.

