Encapsulation Materials Support Semiconductor Reliability

Liquid molding compounds protect semiconductor components during operation and handling. Manufacturers evaluate flow characteristics, curing behavior, adhesion, moisture resistance and warpage control when selecting materials for advanced packages.

These requirements become more demanding as packages incorporate smaller features, denser interconnections and multiple dies.

Advanced Packaging Creates New Material Requirements

Fan-Out Wafer-Level Packaging and ball-grid-array packages are important application areas. Advanced packaging requires materials capable of filling narrow spaces while maintaining dimensional stability and reliability.

Consumer electronics remains a significant end market, while automotive electronics, telecommunications and AI computing create opportunities for specialized formulations.

